<title>ESTONIA: MICROLINK TO SELL WESTERN DIGITAL DISCS.</title>
<headline>MICROLINK TO SELL WESTERN DIGITAL DISCS.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Microlink, the largest computer firm in Estonia, said on Monday it has agreed with Western Digital to sell its hard disks in the Baltic States.</p>
<p>The buyers of Western Digital hard disks are computer makers and after-sale service firms, Microlink said in a statement.</p>
<p>Western Digital is the world's largest manufacturer of computer storage devices such as hard disks, the statement added.</p>
<p>Microlink is an unlisted company that has the largest market share of the Estonian computer market.</p>
<p>-- David Mardiste, Tallinn newsroom +372 630 8400 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
